.\" Made from the kstar help (src/help.rs); do not edit. See src/manual.rs.
.TH KSTAR-LSP 1 "" "Kleene Star" "Kleene Star Manual"
.SH NAME
kstar\-lsp \- the language server editors start (a separate program)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBkstar-lsp\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The Kleene Star language server. An editor starts it and talks to it over
standard input and output with the Language Server Protocol; it is not
meant to be run by hand. It reports errors and warnings as you type, and
gives hover, completion, signature help, go to definition, references,
rename, outline and formatting.
.PP
The VS Code extension starts it for you (\fBkstar update\fR keeps the two
matched). For another editor, configure kstar-lsp as the language server
for .kstar files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help and exit
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
show the version and exit
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBkstar-lsp \-\-version\fR
check which version an editor would start
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBkstar\fR(1)
.PP
The reference and the tutorial: https://github.com/Pratham71/kleene\-star
